<div class="level">
  <div class="level-left">
    <h1 class="title level-item">Settings</h1>
  </div>
</div>

<p class="content">
  Server configuration. Editable fields below take effect on the next apply.
  Structural values (VPN subnet, gateway IP, listen port, interface) are set at
  provisioning time and shown read-only — changing them re-binds the service or
  invalidates every issued client config, so they are deliberately not editable here.
</p>

<h2 class="title is-5">Endpoint &amp; DNS</h2>
<form method="post" action="/settings">
  <%= csrf_tag("/settings") %>

  <div class="field">
    <label class="label">Endpoint host <span class="has-text-grey">(FQDN clients dial; blank = use the raw IP below)</span></label>
    <div class="control">
      <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_host" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_host] %>" placeholder="sg.example.com">
    </div>
    <p class="help">When set, client configs use <code>&lt;host&gt;:<%= @settings[:listen_port] %></code> — move the box by repointing DNS, no config reissue.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="field is-grouped is-grouped-multiline">
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">Endpoint IPv4</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_v4" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_v4] %>" placeholder="203.0.113.5" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">Endpoint IPv6 <span class="has-text-grey">(optional)</span></label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="endpoint_v6" value="<%= @settings[:endpoint_v6] %>" placeholder="2001:db8::5">
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">MTU</label>
      <input class="input" type="number" name="mtu" value="<%= @settings[:mtu] %>" min="1280" max="1500" required>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="field is-grouped is-grouped-multiline">
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">DNS upstream</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="dns_upstream" value="<%= @settings[:dns_upstream] %>" placeholder="1.1.1.1" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">Internal DNS domain</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="dns_domain" value="<%= @settings[:dns_domain] %>" placeholder="vpn" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <label class="label">WAN interface</label>
      <input class="input" type="text" name="wan_interface" value="<%= @settings[:wan_interface] %>" placeholder="eth0" required>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="field">
    <div class="control">
      <button class="button is-primary" type="submit">Save &amp; apply</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>

<hr>

<h2 class="title is-5">Read-only</h2>
<table class="table is-fullwidth">
  <tbody>
    <tr><th>VPN subnet</th><td><code><%= @settings[:wg_subnet] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Gateway IP</th><td><code><%= @settings[:server_ip] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Listen port</th><td><code><%= @settings[:listen_port] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>WireGuard interface</th><td><code><%= @settings[:wg_interface] %></code></td></tr>
    <tr><th>Server public key</th><td><code><%= @settings[:server_pubkey] %></code></td></tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

<hr>

<h2 class="title is-5">Change admin password</h2>
<form method="post" action="/settings/password">
  <%= csrf_tag("/settings/password") %>
  <div class="field is-grouped">
    <div class="control">
      <input class="input" type="password" name="password" placeholder="new password (min 8 chars)" required>
    </div>
    <div class="control">
      <button class="button is-warning" type="submit">Update password</button>
    </div>
  </div>
</form>
